Disable data reporting at compile time -- COMMON half (LW-M1-02).

Split out of upstream's patches/disable-data-reporting-at-compile-time.patch,
which is a straddler: it mixes toolkit/python hunks that are built on every
target with browser/-only hunks. This file holds the target-independent hunks;
patches/disable-data-reporting-desktop.patch holds the browser/ hunk. common +
desktop together are byte-for-byte upstream's current patch.

Both targets build firefox-157.0 (docs/android/TRACK.md, "Decision reversed
2026-10-02"), so this is a common.txt entry again. The Firefox 157 desktop merge
had parked it in desktop.txt, and the mach.txt / glean-core hunks in the desktop
half, while Android stayed on 153esr; both moves are undone.

What is here:
  python/mach/mach/telemetry.py                    mach telemetry, target-independent
  python/sites/mach.txt                            comments out the glean-sdk pypi
                                                   requirement (version in context:
                                                   70.2.0 on 158, 68.0.1 on 157)
  toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Telemetry.cpp  TelemetryImpl never records
  toolkit/library/rust/gkrust-features.mozbuild    glean_disable_upload for official builds
  (Stopwatch.cpp, TelemetryUserInteraction.{cpp,h}: upstream fb4c7a32's
   "no 'cannot be recorded' errors with telemetry off" hunks were dropped in the
   158 rebase - Firefox 158 ships the identical change, IsRecordingEnabled()
   included, so the hunks were already applied and patch refused them.)
  third_party/rust/glean-core/src/lib.rs, third_party/rust/glean-core/src/core/mod.rs
                                                   Glean upload/collection forced off
                                                   inside glean-core (upstream 77f8fcd8,
                                                   which replaced the old
                                                   toolkit/components/glean/src/init/mod.rs
                                                   hunk -- on 157 build_configuration()
                                                   uses a builder and that hunk rejects).
                                                   glean-core is compiled into libxul on
                                                   Android too. It is a vendored crate:
                                                   scripts/librewolf-patches.py rewrites
                                                   the two affected hashes in
                                                   third_party/rust/glean-core/
                                                   .cargo-checksum.json (upstream
                                                   f072d15c) on every target.

WHERE THE ANDROID OFF SWITCH LIVES -- READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THIS PATCH IS
ENOUGH ON ANDROID.

The compile-time data-reporting switch is *not* in this patch. It is
MOZ_DATA_REPORTING, computed at toolkit/moz.configure:3493-3507 as

    telemetry or healthreport or crashreporter or normandy

from four per-project inputs. The front end supplies two of them, and each front
end supplies its own:

  browser/moz.configure:6,10       MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT True, MOZ_NORMANDY True
                                   -> flipped to False by the DESKTOP half.
  mobile/android/moz.configure:131 MOZ_NORMANDY False               (already off)
  mobile/android/moz.configure:132 MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT True   (still ON)

So on Android the common half alone leaves
MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT defined and MOZ_DATA_REPORTING with it. That is
closed by

    patches/android/disable-data-reporting-android.patch   (assets/patches/android.txt)

which must be applied alongside the common half for every Android build. Do not try to
close it from the mozconfig: assets/mozconfig.android's
`mk_add_options MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT=0` is make-level only
(python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozconfig.py routes mk_add_options into make_extra and
never into configure's environment), and an `export` would make configure die on
the implied/explicit conflict with mobile/android/moz.configure:132.

158 rebase (2026-10-04, against Firefox 158.0b3): the Stopwatch.cpp and
TelemetryUserInteraction.{cpp,h} hunks are gone because 158 already contains
them verbatim (patch detected them as "previously applied"). mach.txt's
glean-sdk pin is 70.2.0 on 158; the line is commented out as before. glean-core
is 70.2.0 and the two glean-core hunks are unchanged apart from their position,
so GLEAN_CORE_HASH_FIXUPS in scripts/librewolf-patches.py carries the 158.0b3
pristine and patched sha256 of src/lib.rs and src/core/mod.rs. Telemetry.cpp,
telemetry.py and gkrust-features.mozbuild are unchanged.

